From 5df8d80420571f465d69441969eac44b00060f29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:21:26 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_disks: Device page: disk list with one-line health, a
 page per disk with Monitoring and Report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device (docs/page-design.md 1). kded smart module, D-Bus model, the Ignores/<udi> flag and the report text are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Main page was a column of cards, each with the full health paragraph, Monitor/Ignore and Show Details buttons. It is now a
  ScrollViewKCM list: icon, 'product (path)', one-line summary (Working as expected / Early signs of problems / Failing: back up your
  data now, plus 'not monitored'). Row kcm_disks/DeviceStatus. Clicking a row pushes ui/DevicePage.qml (new).
- DevicePage.qml (Form): Disk, Health, the full explanation (own row, maximumWidth gridUnit*24 so FormLayout stays wide), the list of
  early signs (was a <ul> inside one label), section Monitoring with checkbox 'Warn about problems with this disk' (replaces the
  Monitor/Ignore toggle button, inverted onto device.ignore; row kcm_disks/DeviceMonitor, with a help line), section Report with
  'Show SMART Report…' (was Show Details; row kcm_disks/ShowDetails) opening the unchanged ReportPage (Copy to Clipboard, marker added).
- Toolbar: 'Perform Backup' -> 'Back Up Files…', 'Open Partition Manager' -> 'Open Partition Manager…' (buttons that open something end in …).
- Empty states keep their texts (KdedNotRunning, NoSmartDevices) and now use visible instead of an opacity animation; new BusyIndicator shown
  only if the first GetManagedObjects answer takes over 150 ms. health.js holds the shared wording.
- Relabel: inventory/relabel/kcm_disks.tsv. Inventory --strict: 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-019, HIG-057, HIG-058.

Speed cause (code): nothing blocking in the KCM (devicemodel.cpp reads managed objects with an async watcher; smartctl runs in kded). The
old page built a Card with a banner and a StyledText <ul> for every disk up front; the list row is one light delegate and the report text
is only built on its own page. After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet.
Unconfirmed without a build: required-property names on the delegate (product, path, failed, instabilities, ignore, object) come from
DeviceModel::initRoleNames (QObject property names + 'object'); the model property names are read from the first object, so an empty model has
no roles until a disk appears (as before); health.js is picked up by kcmutils_add_qml_kcm like kcm_bolt's utils.js; the old translated
<ul> string is replaced by plain strings, so those lose translations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
